ng Benny Gantz and Yair Lapid, the party sought to challenge the long-standing dominance of the Likud party and address issues such as security, social equality, and governance. Based in Tel Aviv, the party's formation marked a pivotal moment in Israeli politics, reflecting the shifting allegiances and demographics of the electorate in the contemporary era.

